    <briefdescription>
<para>Truncated-Gaussian push operation, the elementary deformation used by <ref refid="namespacehmap_1abec90e80c5d42318a7aadf6dd1016fec" kindref="member">sls_deformation</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The push adds <computeroutput>amplitude * G(d)</computeroutput> to every vertex within <computeroutput>ir</computeroutput> pixels of the center <computeroutput>(i, j)</computeroutput>, where <computeroutput>G</computeroutput> is a truncated Gaussian kernel equal to 1 at the center and to 0 at distance <computeroutput>ir</computeroutput>. The center vertex is therefore displaced by exactly <computeroutput>amplitude</computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
